<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pan Geng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1300 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pan Geng was a king of the Shang dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, traditionally credited with moving the capital to Yin, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anyang">Anyang</a>, around 1300 BCE. The move ended a series of earlier relocations and Yin remained the capital until the fall of the dynasty. A speech attributed to him is preserved in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-documents">Book of Documents</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pan-geng.jpg" alt="Pan Geng" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 孫家鼐 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%AC%BD%E5%AE%9A%E6%9B%B8%E7%B6%93%E5%9C%96%E8%AA%AA_%E6%96%86%E5%A7%8B%E5%9C%A8%E4%BD%8D%E5%9C%96.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
